# ── Pinning: the files that decide WHICH bytes get built ────────────────────────
# Source-of-truth pins. cookbook.lock and .config together decide whether a recipe is
# compiled from the fork or downloaded prebuilt from static.redox-os.org — both were
# once gitignored, so a fresh clone did not carry them at all; they are tracked as of
# U-168/U-169. Note what that does NOT establish: the same commit producing the same
# image bit for bit is still listed unverified in CLAUDE.md, because the comparison has
# never actually been run. These lines remove an obstacle to reproducibility, not doubt.
# mk/fetch-sha256.txt pins the prebuilt toolchain archives so the compilers that build
# the OS do not rest on TLS alone (U-118). pin-allowlist.txt is the only sanctioned way
# to let a recipe rev sit behind its fork tip, and its steady state is empty.
#
# Cargo.toml / Cargo.lock are in this section and not with the Rust sources because of
# what they pin, not what they are: the root manifest carries six git dependencies, and
# `redox-pkg`'s rev is the SAME commit as `eos-pkgutils`' `pinned_rev` in repos.toml and
# as the pin in recipes/core/pkgutils/recipe.toml. Four files, one commit, and no gate
# compares them — `pin-check` measures repos.toml against the fork tip, not against the
# manifest. A bump that lands in Cargo.toml alone splits the pin and nothing goes red.
/Cargo.toml                        @Gh0s777tt
/Cargo.lock                        @Gh0s777tt
/repos.toml                        @Gh0s777tt
/cookbook.lock                     @Gh0s777tt
/.config                           @Gh0s777tt
