# ── CI, workflows and the gate configuration ────────────────────────────────────
# .github/workflows/ pins every third-party action by 40-char SHA; a diff that shortens
# a pin to a tag is a supply-chain regression that looks like a cleanup. .gitlab-ci.yml
# is still the source-of-truth pipeline. deny.toml / osv-scanner.toml hold the
# suppression lists — an added exception is an argument, not a config tweak.
#
# ci-integrity.sh is listed, and so are the two files it delegates to: checks 6 and 7 do
# not reach their own verdict, they run eos-source-rules.sh and eos-check-repo-types.py
# and read a verdict LINE off each (U-177). Owning the gate but not the instrument leaves
# the editable half — the half that could be made to always print OK — unowned.
# .gitattributes is check 8's reference copy; those line endings were changed once and
# had to be spotted and reverted by hand (U-169). setup-github-security.sh is the odd one
# out: it is the only file here that writes state living in GitHub's database — rulesets,
# the Actions allowlist, secret scanning — which is precisely the state that cannot be
# reviewed as a diff afterwards.
